WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.835
Zann and Perda scurried out of the tree trunk.

2
00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:07.701
The forest was dark and spooky, and Zann didn't want to go any deeper into it.

3
00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:11.703
Besides, he didn't want to get too far from the wormhole.

4
00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:16.111
"Look, a cave!" Perda pointed. "Let's hide in there."

5
00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:24.016
At the cave's entrance, Zann used the small amount of energy he had left to do a quick Life Force Locator spell.

6
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:27.550
The cave was empty, so he and Perda huddled inside.

7
00:00:27.551 --> 00:00:35.003
As the two monsters continued to fight outside, Zann and Perda caught their breath and talked about what had happened.

8
00:00:35.004 --> 00:00:39.948
"Did you see whether Darb, Gliss, and Zing stayed together?" Zann asked.

9
00:00:39.949 --> 00:00:45.872
"I couldn't tell." Perda looked worried. "If Darb gets separated from Gliss . . ."

10
00:00:45.873 --> 00:00:50.637
"I know. Without magic, he'd be helpless in the vortex."

11
00:00:50.638 --> 00:00:56.784
Zann's mind flashed again to Venna. What had become of her? And what about Morb?

12
00:00:56.785 --> 00:01:01.112
Without his stolen magic, he was a Void, just like Darb.

13
00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:05.908
"We need to figure out how to find them," Perda said. "Fast!"

14
00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:09.146
"How?" Zann glanced out of the cave.

15
00:01:09.147 --> 00:01:16.412
"Even if we can make it past those two monsters and back to the wormhole, we can't even navigate our way through the vortex.

16
00:01:16.413 --> 00:01:20.710
Let alone find our friends." He looked at Perda.

17
00:01:20.711 --> 00:01:24.767
"I can't believe I dragged you all into this," he mumbled.

18
00:01:24.768 --> 00:01:29.387
Perda shrugged. "You didn't drag me—I wanted to come."

19
00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:38.357
Zann gave a small chuckle. "Well, we've both said we want to be explorers. Now here we are—exploring."

20
00:01:38.358 --> 00:01:44.886
Perda peered out from the cave and then smiled. "Look! They're running off!"

21
00:01:44.887 --> 00:01:51.904
Zann looked out. The battling monsters had stopped fighting and were now racing away in opposite directions.

22
00:01:51.905 --> 00:01:56.079
"That's weird," he said. "I wonder why they're leaving."

23
00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.228
"Who cares?" said Perda. "This could be our chance to get back to the wormhole."

24
00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.075
She crawled out of the cave. "Come on!"

25
00:02:05.076 --> 00:02:10.799
They raced out of the forest and across the dark plain, dodging random bursts of energy.

26
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.081
Zann could see the wormhole winking at them just ahead.

27
00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:16.875
Being in the vortex was pretty scary.

28
00:02:16.876 --> 00:02:20.898
But they'd just discovered that certain worlds were even scarier.

29
00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:25.300
"Hurry!" he called to Perda. "We have to—argh!"

30
00:02:25.301 --> 00:02:32.473
Zann suddenly felt a stinging sensation, as if he were being stuck with burning needles all over his body.

31
00:02:32.474 --> 00:02:35.820
He fell to the ground, twitching and groaning.

32
00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:39.588
"What's happening?" Perda cried in a shaky voice.

33
00:02:39.589 --> 00:02:44.486
Out of the corner of his eye, Zann saw her fall, twitching, beside him.

34
00:02:44.487 --> 00:02:47.370
Then a new creature stepped into view.

35
00:02:47.371 --> 00:02:54.326
It was much smaller than the dragon or the deca-stinger—in fact, it wasn't much bigger than Zing. It

36
00:02:54.327 --> 00:02:59.903
didn't look very scary either. It resembled a hairy walking mop. Even

37
00:02:59.904 --> 00:03:07.398
so, Zann shivered when he saw it. "Oh no," he said. "It's a scatter beast!" "

38
00:03:07.399 --> 00:03:13.802
That's a scatter beast?" Perda said. "The thing that knocked your parents off

39
00:03:13.803 --> 00:03:20.346
course?" Zann couldn't answer. As the scatter beast crept closer, the stinging sensations grew

40
00:03:20.347 --> 00:03:25.248
worse. Besides, Zann didn't know much more about scatter beasts than Perda

41
00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:31.183
did. All he knew was that they threw off chaotic energy that confused the magic of

42
00:03:31.184 --> 00:03:35.294
others. He struggled to regain control of his body, but it was no

43
00:03:35.295 --> 00:03:44.516
use. The scatter beast was still approaching. A skinny tentacle appeared from amid the dirty, grayish hair and stretched toward the

44
00:03:44.517 --> 00:03:50.730
kids. Zann could only stare at it, mesmerized by the spiral-shaped claw at the

45
00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:56.374
end. "We have to get away!" Perda cried. She rubbed her hands together.

46
00:03:56.375 --> 00:04:00.107
"Blast!" A small sizzle of energy spit out of her

47
00:04:00.108 --> 00:04:05.192
hand. It made it halfway to the scatter beast before suddenly doubling back toward the

48
00:04:05.193 --> 00:04:08.938
kids. At the same time, it swelled into a

49
00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:12.580
fireball. "Look out!" Zann yelled, throwing himself

50
00:04:12.581 --> 00:04:15.283
aside. Perda rolled away just in time

51
00:04:15.284 --> 00:04:19.936
too. The fireball blasted a large hole in the rocky ground between

52
00:04:19.937 --> 00:04:23.064
them. Zann tried to turn to make sure Perda was

53
00:04:23.065 --> 00:04:28.573
okay. But he couldn't move anymore. He realized he'd thrown himself even closer to the scatter

54
00:04:28.574 --> 00:04:36.799
beast. All Zann could do now was stare helplessly as the creature moved toward him, its claw aimed at his

55
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.069
forehead. Zann knew he should be scared. After all, he was about to

56
00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.770
die. But instead the only thing he felt was

57
00:04:45.771 --> 00:04:51.837
regret. He regretted that he would never find his parents, that Boz would never know what had happened to

58
00:04:51.838 --> 00:04:58.387
him, and that he'd never have the chance to make up with Gliss—or even find out if she and the others had survived . . .

59
00:04:58.388 --> 00:05:03.321
Then, out of the corner of his eye, he noticed something strange.

60
00:05:03.322 --> 00:05:10.603
A sparkling rain of colorful glitter was falling gently from the sky, seemingly out of nowhere.

61
00:05:10.604 --> 00:05:17.031
At first Zann assumed it was an illusion, that the scatter beast's energy was affecting his vision.

62
00:05:17.032 --> 00:05:21.504
Then the first bits of glitter touched the scatter beast.

63
00:05:21.505 --> 00:05:27.946
They sizzled and burned some of its fur, causing the beast to jump back and howl with pain.

64
00:05:27.947 --> 00:05:35.402
Its wild energy went even wilder, sparking fires here and there and making the ground shudder.

65
00:05:35.403 --> 00:05:39.068
"Huh?" Zann mumbled through numb lips.

66
00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:44.869
Then he felt someone grab him by the arm and drag him across the hard, rocky ground.

67
00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.827
A moment later he felt the increasingly familiar sensation of passing through a wormhole.

68
00:05:50.828 --> 00:05:54.443
The vortex felt almost welcoming after Fardark.

69
00:05:54.444 --> 00:05:58.298
When he felt Perda bump against him, Zann was relieved.

70
00:05:58.299 --> 00:06:02.317
They'd both made it out. But who had rescued them?

71
00:06:02.318 --> 00:06:06.445
"That was close," an irritated voice snapped.

72
00:06:06.446 --> 00:06:10.805
"I thought I warned you about the wormholes, boy."

73
00:06:10.806 --> 00:06:14.567
Zann blinked, his vision swimming back into focus.

74
00:06:14.568 --> 00:06:19.517
He gasped as he finally got a good look at the person who had grabbed him.

75
00:06:19.518 --> 00:06:24.233
It was Wyssa!

